Author: leslieleesoftwareengineer <80076295+leslieleesoftwareengineer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Tue Sep 15 23:09:01 2026 +1000

    R-9: add mission creation to the SPA (New Mission button + form)

    The backend/CLI already let Director or Mission Lead create missions
    (require_role on POST /missions) -- the SPA just never had a form for
    it, for either role. Not a permissions bug, a scope gap left over from
    Q16/Q17's "not full CLI parity" SPA scoping.

    Adds api.mission.create, a MissionCreateScreen (name/description/
    start/end date, client-side end>=start check mirroring the API's own
    validator), and a "New Mission" button on the mission list, wired in
    as a third state alongside list/detail (still no router).

    Verified live in the browser as a Mission Lead: created a mission,
    watched it land in the list and land on its detail screen. Typecheck,
    lint, and the full backend suite (137 tests) all green.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PweKuPVuVn2wxp2XGb4nFm

